\ A raise reached through a tail-position `when`, pinned interpreted. The interpreter tail-calls
\ `when` and pops its frame, so the chain carries no combinator row. That chain is the target
\ every tier converges on.
\
\ The eager twins are eager_tail_boundary_compiled_caller.1z, where only `go` compiles, and
\ eager_tail_boundary_compiled_both.1z, where `boom` compiles too. `boom` declares its effect here
\ because every AOT build requires one; the interpreted chain is the same without it. The AOT
\ suite builds this file through `.source` redirects with their own goldens.

boom: ( -- ) [ f "kaboom" EUserThrown make-error throw ] ;
go: ( ? -- ) [ [ boom ] when ] ;

[ t go ] [ inspect print-line ] recover
